# Apex formatting

- Format every changed Apex file with the repository's configured Prettier Apex plugin.
- Put spaces around assignment and binary operators and after commas.
- Put spaces inside collection initializer braces, for example `new Set<Id>{ recordId }`.
- Use one statement per line.
- Leave at least one blank line between the end of one method body and the next method declaration or annotation.
- Always wrap the body of `if`, `else`, `for`, `while`, and similar control-flow statements in braces, even when the body contains one statement.
- Never place the controlled statement on the same line as its condition.

```apex
if (condition) {
  doLogic();
}
```
